-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate MGCenter Complete Eq Op Tensor Avg
-- statement:
--   **The complete-part M-G center equals an averaged tensor-product expectation.**
--
--   For an indexed polynomial family and projective submeasurement `M`, let $C_{MG}$ be the average middle-sandwich expectation using the complete-part family and the total effect of `M`. Over the uniform slice-pair distribution, it has the equivalent operator-tensor form
--
--   $$
--   C_{MG}=\mathbb E_{q}\,\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{bi}}\!\left(\operatorname{opTensor}\left(M_{q.2}^{\mathrm{tot}},G_{q.1}^{\mathrm{tot}}\right)\right).
--   $$
--
--   Here $G_{q.1}^{\mathrm{tot}}$ is the complete-part total associated with the first slice coordinate, and $M_{q.2}^{\mathrm{tot}}$ is the total of `M` on the second coordinate. This exact rewrite identifies the common center with the aggregate operator expression used by the switcheroo theorem.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateMGCenterComplete_eq_opTensor_avg`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
